Input: {"question": "Inquiry about the residence would be: \"Where does Jenny Bach reside?\"", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 63, "text": "Title: The Munich Connection: Unraveling the Life of Jenny Bach"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 65, "end": 178, "text": "In the heart of Bavaria, Germany, lies the vibrant city of Munich, a hub of cultural and historical significance."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 179, "end": 351, "text": "It is here, amidst the bustling streets and picturesque landscapes, that our story unfolds, centered around the life of Jenny Bach, a Holocaust victim born on May 17, 1866."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 352, "end": 458, "text": "As we delve into the life of Jenny, we find ourselves transported to a time of great turmoil and upheaval."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 459, "end": 615, "text": "The late 19th century was marked by significant social, economic, and political changes in Germany, which would ultimately shape the course of Jenny's life."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 616, "end": 750, "text": "Munich, with its rich cultural heritage and strong Jewish community, became a beacon of hope for many, including Jenny and her family."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 751, "end": 913, "text": "One of the earliest pieces of evidence that supports Jenny's residence in Munich is a birth certificate, dated May 17, 1866, which confirms her birth in the city."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 914, "end": 1009, "text": "This document, now yellowed with age, provides a tangible link to Jenny's early life in Munich."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1010, "end": 1159, "text": "The certificate, issued by the Munich City Council, bears the official seal of the city, further solidifying the connection between Jenny and Munich."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1160, "end": 1244, "text": "As Jenny grew up, she became an integral part of Munich's thriving Jewish community."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1245, "end": 1377, "text": "The city's synagogues, cultural institutions, and community centers played a significant role in shaping her identity and worldview."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1378, "end": 1556, "text": "A letter written by Jenny's rabbi, dated 1885, mentions her active participation in the Munich Jewish Community Center's charity events, demonstrating her deep roots in the city."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1557, "end": 1620, "text": "Jenny's life in Munich was not without its challenges, however."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1621, "end": 1785, "text": "The late 19th and early 20th centuries saw a rise in anti-Semitic sentiment in Germany, which would eventually culminate in the devastating events of the Holocaust."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1786, "end": 1991, "text": "A newspaper article from the Münchner Neueste Nachrichten, dated 1923, reports on a series of anti-Semitic incidents in Munich, highlighting the growing tensions and hostility towards the Jewish community."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1992, "end": 2086, "text": "This article serves as a poignant reminder of the precarious environment in which Jenny lived."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2087, "end": 2168, "text": "Despite the challenges, Jenny remained deeply connected to Munich and its people."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2169, "end": 2336, "text": "A testimonial from a family friend, written in 1940, describes Jenny's love for the city's traditional Bavarian cuisine and her favorite haunts in the historic center."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2337, "end": 2463, "text": "This personal account humanizes Jenny, providing a glimpse into her daily life and her attachment to the city she called home."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 14, "text": "**Jenny Bach**"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 16, "end": 183, "text": "Jenny Bach (May 17, 1866 – unknown) was a Czech Jewish woman who resided in the village of Holubov, located in the Český Krumlov District of the South Bohemian region."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 184, "end": 223, "text": "**Early Life and Residency in Holubov**"}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 225, "end": 334, "text": "Jenny Bach was born on May 17, 1866, in the Austro-Hungarian Empire, which is now part of the Czech Republic."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 335, "end": 481, "text": "According to the 1880 census of the Český Krumlov District, Bach resided in Holubov with her family, where they operated a small textile business."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 482, "end": 485, "text": "[1]"}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 487, "end": 511, "text": "**Studies and Research**"}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 513, "end": 759, "text": "A 2010 study published in the Journal of Czech History found that during the late 19th century, Holubov experienced a significant influx of Jewish immigrants, including the Bach family, who contributed to the local economy and cultural landscape."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 760, "end": 801, "text": "[2] The study, conducted by historian Dr."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 802, "end": 930, "text": "Eva Nováková, analyzed census data and archival records to reconstruct the demographic changes in the region during this period."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 931, "end": 1133, "text": "In 2015, a team of researchers from the University of South Bohemia conducted an oral history project in Holubov, collecting testimonies from local residents about their experiences during World War II."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1134, "end": 1288, "text": "One of the interviewees, a 95-year-old woman named Anna Šťastná, recalled her childhood memories of Jenny Bach, who lived in the village during the 1930s."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1289, "end": 1292, "text": "[3]"}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1294, "end": 1308, "text": "**References**"}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1310, "end": 1351, "text": "[1] Český Krumlov District Census (1880)."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1352, "end": 1379, "text": "Archiv města Český Krumlov."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1380, "end": 1396, "text": "[2] Nováková, E."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1397, "end": 1404, "text": "(2010)."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1405, "end": 1481, "text": "\"Jewish Immigration to the Český Krumlov District in the Late 19th Century.\""}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1482, "end": 1521, "text": "Journal of Czech History, 28(1), 35-50."}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1522, "end": 1554, "text": "[3] University of South Bohemia."}, "D2S22": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1555, "end": 1562, "text": "(2015)."}, "D2S23": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1563, "end": 1613, "text": "Oral History Project: Holubov during World War II."}, "D2S24": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1614, "end": 1637, "text": "Unpublished manuscript."}}, "candidates": [], "original_cards": [], "initial_answers": ["Munich", "Holubov"]}
